{"request_uuid": "caacdd4d-ad99-478a-ba94-72fe26930973", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T14:42:14.066907+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "mode": "patch", "workspace_folder": "loan-payments", "mac_id": "5c:9b:a6:82:ff:92", "type": "turn_end", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "No git repo? `git rev-parse` exited 127 meaning git not found? Let me check. Actually code 127 command not found. So git isn't installed. That's why run-tests.sh's `git rev-parse` falls back to ROOT=\".\". And the setup guard `git submodule update` would fail... but data-catalog exists.\n\nActually wait, ROOT computation: \n```\nP=\"${SQRL_PACKAGE_PREFIX:-}\"\nif [ -n \"$P\" ]; then ROOT=...\nelif ROOT=\"$(git rev-parse --show-prefix 2>/dev/null)\"; then ...\nelse ROOT=\".\"\nfi\n```\nIf git absent, `git rev-parse` returns 127 (command not found), the elif fails, ROOT=\".\". Good.\n\nNow, the final line request: \"Your last action must be a successful run of `./run-tests.sh`, scoped with the names of every affected sub-projects.\" Since I add a dev overlay, I should test compile with dev. But run-tests.sh doesn't have a way to compile only loan-payments with dev unless we select it. Final invocation could be `./run-tests.sh loan-payments` (test) plus maybe compile. The template says output exact invocation. I'll run `./run-tests.sh loan-payments` presumably. But I also want to verify `--compile --env dev`. Hmm, the requirement specifically wants `./run-tests.sh --compile --env dev` to compile loan-payments. Let me make that work.\n\nKey question: should `loan-payments_table_test/dev` be declared? Let me think about the design intent from the reference. In the reference finance-demo, maybe SUBPROJECTS = \"loan-payments loan-payments_table_test\" and ENVS = \"test prod dev\"? If so, they must have a table_test/dev suite. Let me reason what it'd be.\n\nActually, maybe the reference project has only `loan-payments` subproject? But our project inventory says SUBPROJECTS has two. The request says \"compiles the loan-payments sub-project\" specifically, not table_test. Perhaps the intended run-tests.sh change maps dev only for loan-payments, and the `--env dev` with no subproject only runs loan-payments? No, the loop runs all.\n\nWait, maybe they intend that `--env dev` requires selecting the subproject? But the requirement explicitly writes `./run-tests.sh --compile --env dev` without subproject. Hmm.\n\nLet me reconsider: Perhaps the cleanest solution consistent with \"compiles the loan-payments sub-project\" is to add suite entries for dev for both sub-projects. For `loan-payments_table_test/dev`, use `loan-payments-shared-package.json loan-payments-table-test-package.json`? But that uses test package for dev. That seems wrong/surprising. Alternatively `loan-payments-shared-package.json loan-payments-dev-package.json` for both. But then table_test/dev would not have test-runner. For compile that's fine and it reads test data. Actually the dev overlay semantics \"reads the catalog test data (environment test)\". The table_test subproject is just a test harness. For dev local run you wouldn't use table_test.\n\nHmm. Let me look at how the DataSQRL \"run-tests.sh\" template handles dev in other reference examples. Search the whole filesystem for run-tests.sh with dev env.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning_content"}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20e01d79c72639cdf9740", "name": "bash", "arguments": {"command": "grep -rln 'ENVS=\"test prod dev\"\\|ENVS=\"test dev\"\\|dev)' /opt /workspace /root 2>/dev/null | grep -v build | head -20; echo \"=== all run-tests.sh ===\"; find / -path /proc -prune -o -name run-tests.sh -print 2>/dev/null | head"}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "together", "model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash", "usage": {"input": 125, "output": 852, "cacheRead": 35456, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 733, "totalTokens": 36433, "cost": {"input": 3.75e-05, "output": 0.0010224, "cacheRead": 0.000212736,