{"request_uuid": "caacdd4d-ad99-478a-ba94-72fe26930973", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T14:42:57.605805+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "mode": "patch", "workspace_folder": "loan-payments", "mac_id": "5c:9b:a6:82:ff:92", "type": "message_start", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_01a20e0283017702a704fa75", "toolName": "edit", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced 6 block(s) in /workspace/loan-payments/README.md."}], "details": {"diff": "     ...\n  34 | `Personal_Loan` | `testdata/consumer_loans-personal_loan.jsonl` | Kafka topic `consumer_loans.personal_loan` |\n  35 | `Loan_Payment` | `testdata/consumer_loans-loan_payment.jsonl` | Kafka topic `consumer_loans.loan_payment` |\n  36 \n  37 Both are CDC streams with `ingested_at` watermarks (10 s in test, 30 s in prod). The project uses\n- 38 the catalog watermarks as they are. The catalog's other consumer-loan tables \u2014 `Auto_Loan`,\n+ 38 the catalog watermarks as they are. The `dev` overlay sets `environment: test`, so a local\n+ 39 development run reads the same filesystem test data as the test suites. The catalog's other consumer-loan tables \u2014 `Auto_Loan`,\n  39 `Loan_Application` and `Consumer_Loan_Delinquency_Event` \u2014 are intentionally out of scope: the\n  40 project neither reads nor tests them.\n  41 \n  42 ## Architecture and Implementation Choices\n     ...\n  95 Every query needs a valid JWT with the top-level claim `customer_id`; a request without a valid\n  96 token is rejected (`JWT auth failed` / `Unauthorized`). The claim is mapped to a required function\n  97 argument with `METADATA FROM 'auth.customer_id'`.\n  98 \n- 99 The auth provider is configured under `engines.vertx.config.auth` in each test and prod overlay:\n+100 The auth provider is configured under `engines.vertx.config.auth` in each test, dev and prod\n+101 overlay:\n 100 \n 101 - **test**: issuer `loan-payments-test-issuer`, audience `loan-payments-test-audience`, inline HS256\n 102   key from the fixed secret `dummy-super-secret-jwt-signing-string` (base64url without padding:\n 103   `ZHVtbXktc3VwZXItc2VjcmV0LWp3dC1zaWduaW5nLXN0cmluZw`).\n+106 - **dev**: issuer `loan-payments-issuer`, audience `loan-payments-api`, inline HS256 key from the\n+107   fixed dev secret `loan-payments-test-secret-signing-string` (base64url without padding:\n+108   `bG9hbi1wYXltZW50cy10ZXN0LXNlY3JldC1zaWduaW5nLXN0cmluZw`).\n 104 - **prod**: issuer `${AUTH_ISSUER}`, audience `${AUTH_AUDIENCE}`, key `${JWT_SECRET}` (base64url).\n 105 \n 106 Mint a test token for any customer id:\n 107 \n     ...\n 181 \u251c\u2500\u2500 loan-payments.sqrl                        # processing, lookups and table tests\n 182 \u251c\u2500\u2500 loan-payments-shared-package.json         # base config: engines, catalog include, API\n 183 \u251c\u2500\u2500 loan-payments-api-test-package.json       # custom-schema API tests\n 184 \u251c\u2500\u2500 loan-payments-table-test-package.json     # inferred-schema table tests\n+190 \u251c\u2500\u2500 loan-payments-dev-package.json            # local development auth (test catalog data)\n 185 \u251c\u2500\u2500 loan-payments-prod-package.json           # production auth\n 186 \u251c\u2500\u2500 loan-payments-api/\n 187 \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 schema.v1.graphqls                    # GraphQL schema\n 188 \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 operations.v1.graphql                 # REST/MCP operations\n     ...\n 203 cd loan-payments                             # the project folder, from the repository root\n 204 ./run-tests.sh                               # run the API tests and the table tests\n 205 ./run-tests.sh loan-payments                 # run only the API tests\n 206 ./run-tests.sh loan-payments_table_test      # run only the table tests\n+213 ./run-tests.sh --compile --env dev loan-payments    # compile the local dev pipeline\n 207 ./run-tests.sh --compile --env prod loan-payments   # compile the production pipeline\n 208 ```\n 209 \n 210 The `docker run` commands make the same DataSQRL calls and work from any folder inside the git\n 211 repository.\n 212 \n 213 ```bash\n 214 docker run --rm -v \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\":/workspace datasqrl/cmd:0.12.5 \\\n+222   compile -r loan-payments loan-payments-shared-package.json loan-payments-dev-package.json -b loan-payments\n+223 docker run --rm -v \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\":/workspace datasqrl/cmd:0.12.5 \\\n 215   compile -r loan-payments loan-payments-shared-package.json loan-payments-prod-package.json -b loan-payments\n 216 docker run -it --rm -v \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\":/workspace datasqrl/cmd:0.12.5 \\\n 217   test -r loan-payments loan-payments-shared-package.json loan-payments-api-test-package.json -b loan-payments\n 218 docker run -it --rm -v \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\":/workspace datasqrl/cmd:0.12.5 \\\n     ...\n 220 ```\n 221 \n 222 `-b <name>` writes the output to `build/<name>`, and it is optional.\n 223 \n-224 The project has no `dev` environment; the `test` environment reads the catalog's filesystem test data\n-225 and can be used for a local run:\n+233 The `dev` overlay is the local development environment. It reads the catalog's filesystem test data\n+234 (`environment: test`) and signs with a fixed dev issuer, audience and HS256 key, so no production\n+235 credentials are needed. Layer it over the base for a local run:\n 226 \n 227 ```bash\n 228 docker run -it --rm -p 8888:8888 -p 8081:8081 -v \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\":/workspace datasqrl/cmd:0.12.5 \\\n-229   run -r loan-payments loan-payments-shared-package.json loan-payments-api-test-package.json\n+239   run -r loan-payments loan-payments-shared-package.json loan-payments-dev-package.json\n 230 ```\n 231 \n 232 While the pipeline runs: the Flink WebUI is at http://localhost:8081/, the GraphQL API and GraphiQL\n 233 at http://localhost:8888/v1/graphiql/, the REST Swagger UI at http://localhost:8888/v1/swagger-ui,\n     ...", "patch": "--- /workspace/loan-payments/README.md\n+++ /workspace/loan-payments/README.md\n@@ -34,9 +34,10 @@\n | `Personal_Loan` | `testdata/consumer_loans-personal_loan.jsonl` | Kafka topic `consumer_loans.personal_loan` |\n | `Loan_Payment` | `testdata/consumer_loans-loan_payment.jsonl` | Kafka topic `consumer_loans.loan_payment` |\n \n Both are CDC streams with `ingested_at` watermarks (10 s in test, 30 s in prod). The project uses\n-the catalog watermarks as they are. The catalog's other consumer-loan tables \u2014 `Auto_Loan`,\n+the catalog watermarks as they are. The `dev` overlay sets `environment: test`, so a local\n+development run reads the same filesystem test data as the test suites. The catalog's other consumer-loan tables \u2014 `Auto_Loan`,\n `Loan_Application` and `Consumer_Loan_Delinquency_Event` \u2014 are intentionally out of scope: the\n project neither reads nor tests them.\n \n ## Architecture and Implementation Choices\n@@ -95,13 +96,17 @@\n Every query needs a valid JWT with the top-level claim `customer_id`; a request without a valid\n token is rejected (`JWT auth failed` / `Unauthorized`). The claim is mapped to a required function\n argument with `METADATA FROM 'auth.customer_id'`.\n \n-The auth provider is configured under `engines.vertx.config.auth` in each test and prod overlay:\n+The auth provider is configured under `engines.vertx.config.auth` in each test, dev and prod\n+overlay:\n \n - **test**: issuer `loan-payments-test-issuer`, audience `loan-payments-test-audience`, inline HS256\n   key from the fixed secret `dummy-super-secret-jwt-signing-string` (base64url without padding:\n   `ZHVtbXktc3VwZXItc2VjcmV0LWp3dC1zaWduaW5nLXN0cmluZw`).\n+- **dev**: issuer `loan-payments-issuer`, audience `loan-payments-api`, inline HS256 key from the\n+  fixed dev secret `loan-payments-test-secret-signing-string` (base64url without padding:\n+  `bG9hbi1wYXltZW50cy10ZXN0LXNlY3JldC1zaWduaW5nLXN0cmluZw`).\n - **prod**: issuer `${AUTH_ISSUER}`, audience `${AUTH_AUDIENCE}`, key `${JWT_